  "evidence": "Original SwissWatchExpo stock 84933 explicitly identifies numeric 126715; gallery 7 shows the same case engraving. Its photographed card identifies 126715CHNR and tag M126715CHNR-0001 (gallery 12); paperwork inspected for identification only and excluded from the gallery. Stock 77501 identifies 126715CHNR and its case engraving reads 126715; no full retail suffix established for that specimen. All 25 original gallery files inspected, selected views separately inspected at high resolution. Both opened movement photographs visibly show 3285 and 31 jewels, with differing rotor executions. These are specimen comparisons, not a dated revision chronology, interchangeable-part proof or authentication of the user watch. Rolex original -0001 brochure specifies 40 mm 18 ct Everose, black dial, brown/black Cerachrom, automatic GMT 3285, approximately 70-hour reserve, Oyster bracelet and Oysterlock/Easylink. Dealer dates do not establish production intervals. No -0002 photograph inheritance, neighbouring reference, generic calibre substitute, inner caseback or individual material authenticity inferred.",
